# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Introduction {#introduction}"
msgstr "Panimula {#introduction}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The world is approaching the era of quantum advantage. Here, quantum advantage refers to executing a task on a hybrid quantum–classical system such that:\n"
"* The correctness of the output can be rigorously verified.\n"
"* The computation demonstrates a quantum separation &mdash; providing superior efficiency, cost-effectiveness, or accuracy compared with classical methods alone.\n"
msgstr ""
"Papalapit na ang mundo sa panahon ng quantum advantage. Dito, ang quantum advantage ay tumutukoy sa pagsasagawa ng isang task sa isang hybrid quantum–classical system kung saan:\n"
"* Ang kawastuhan ng output ay mahigpit na maaaring i-verify.\n"
"* Ipinapakita ng computation ang isang quantum separation &mdash; na nagbibigay ng mas mahusay na efficiency, cost-effectiveness, o accuracy kumpara sa classical methods lamang.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Reaching quantum advantage in the near term will require us to use every available tool to get the most out of today’s quantum hardware. In practice, that means confronting noise and errors head-on.\n"
"We have an ever-expanding toolkit to address these challenges, including error suppression, error mitigation, error detection, and error correction. These concepts can be difficult to distinguish, in part because they lie along a continuum on the path toward fault-tolerant quantum computing. Roughly speaking:\n"
"* Error suppression aims to reduce the probability of certain errors occurring in the first place.\n"
"* Error mitigation seeks to reduce the impact of errors that have occurred on the final result.\n"
"* Error detection and correction encode quantum information redundantly across multiple qubits, so that errors can be detected and corrected through consistency checks.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pag-abot sa quantum advantage sa malapit na hinaharap ay mangangailangan sa atin na gamitin ang bawat available na tool upang makuha ang pinakamahusay mula sa quantum hardware ngayon. Sa praktika, nangangahulugan ito ng direktang pagharap sa noise at errors.\n"
"Mayroon tayong patuloy na lumalawak na toolkit para tugunan ang mga hamong ito, kabilang ang error suppression, error mitigation, error detection, at error correction. Ang mga konseptong ito ay maaaring mahirap ihiwalay, bahagi dahil ang mga ito ay nasa isang continuum sa landas patungo sa fault-tolerant quantum computing. Sa pangkalahatan:\n"
"* Layunin ng error suppression na bawasan ang posibilidad na mangyari ang ilang errors sa unang pagkakataon.\n"
"* Layunin ng error mitigation na bawasan ang epekto ng mga errors na nangyari sa huling resulta.\n"
"* Ang error detection at correction ay nag-eencode ng quantum information nang paulit-ulit sa maraming qubits, upang ang mga errors ay ma-detect at maitama sa pamamagitan ng consistency checks.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Image of errors being reduced by error suppression, then correction, then mitigation.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/intro/error-handling.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Image of errors being reduced by error suppression, then correction, then mitigation.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/intro/error-handling.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Some techniques blur these boundaries. For example, if errors can be detected at the circuit level and invalid shots are discarded or probabilistically recovered in post-processing, this may be viewed as a limited form of error correction, though it lacks the full fault-tolerant structure of quantum error-correcting codes.\n"
msgstr "May mga technique na nagpapalabo sa mga hangganang ito. Halimbawa, kung ang mga error ay ma-detect sa antas ng circuit at ang mga invalid shot ay itinatapon o probabilistic na na-recover sa post-processing, ito ay maaaring ituring bilang isang limitadong anyo ng error correction, bagama't kulang ito sa buong fault-tolerant structure ng quantum error-correcting codes.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli twirling, another example, reshapes noise so that it behaves like a stochastic Pauli process. This can slow the buildup of coherent errors and make other techniques, such as error mitigation, more effective. On its own, however, it is best described as a form of noise tailoring, rather than strictly suppression or mitigation.\n"
msgstr "Ang Pauli twirling, isa pang halimbawa, ay bumubuo muli sa noise upang kumilos ito tulad ng isang stochastic Pauli process. Maaari nitong pabagalin ang pag-ipon ng coherent errors at gawing mas epektibo ang ibang mga technique, tulad ng error mitigation. Gayunpaman, sa sarili nito, mas tamang ilarawan ito bilang isang anyo ng noise tailoring, kaysa sa mahigpit na suppression o mitigation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These tools are not mutually exclusive. Effective workflows often combine multiple approaches. Suppression and mitigation are widely applicable today, while error detection can be used in some workflows to discard erroneous results or probabilistically recover correct states. Meanwhile, increasingly advanced forms of error correction are steadily coming within reach. By leveraging and combining these methods, we can build a continuous path toward fault-tolerant quantum computing. For a streamlined approach to leveraging multiple error mitigation techniques, without much theoretical background, see [this tutorial](/tutorials/combine-error-mitigation-techniques) on IBM Quantum&reg; Platform.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga tool na ito ay hindi mutually exclusive. Ang mga epektibong workflow ay kadalasang pinagsasama ang maraming approach. Ang suppression at mitigation ay malawakang applicable ngayon, habang ang error detection ay maaaring gamitin sa ilang workflow upang itapon ang mga maling resulta o probabilistic na ma-recover ang tamang states. Samantala, ang lalong umuunlad na mga anyo ng error correction ay unti-unting nalalapit na maabot. Sa paggamit at pagsasama ng mga method na ito, maaari tayong bumuo ng tuluy-tuloy na landas patungo sa fault-tolerant quantum computing. Para sa isang streamlined na approach sa paggamit ng maraming error mitigation technique, nang walang masyadong theoretical background, tingnan ang [tutorial na ito](/tutorials/combine-error-mitigation-techniques) sa IBM Quantum&reg; Platform.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this course, Tools for Quantum Advantage, we will explore some of the most promising methods for managing quantum noise and errors. Our focus is on exploring practical applications using Qiskit, while providing enough theoretical background to help you determine which techniques are appropriate for your use case. We will also highlight which methods can be combined effectively within a single workflow &mdash; and which ones typically cannot.\n"
msgstr "Sa kursong ito, Tools for Quantum Advantage, sisiyasatin natin ang ilan sa mga pinaka-promising na method para sa pamamahala ng quantum noise at errors. Ang ating pokus ay sa pagsisiyasat ng mga praktikal na aplikasyon gamit ang Qiskit, habang nagbibigay ng sapat na theoretical background upang matulungan kang matukoy kung aling mga technique ang angkop para sa iyong use case. Itatampok din natin kung aling mga method ang maaaring pagsamahin nang epektibo sa loob ng iisang workflow &mdash; at kung alin naman ang karaniwang hindi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Join us as we explore the tools that will help bring quantum advantage within reach.\n"
msgstr "Sumama sa amin habang sinisiyasat natin ang mga tool na makakatulong upang maabot ang quantum advantage.\n"
